{
	"_comment": "The plaintext the phone seals for a scheduled send, byte for byte as ScheduledSendOps.drainPending writes it through org.json (keys in insertion order, a slash escaped), with files from fileJson in MessageFile.kt. `decoded` is what the plaintext holds. `wire` is the ChannelFile list an ordinary send carries for the same files, the phone's OutgoingFile.wireFile and its TypeScript twin scheduledWireFile; a file with no size has no wire form. Read by inbox-delivery-pump.test.ts; a Kotlin test pins fileJson and wireFile to the same file.",
	"cases": [
		{
			"name": "text-only",
			"plaintext": "{\"text\":\"Check the deploy\",\"messageId\":\"sched-1\",\"files\":[]}",
			"decoded": { "text": "Check the deploy", "messageId": "sched-1", "files": [] },
			"wire": []
		},
		{
			"name": "slash-escaped",
			"plaintext": "{\"text\":\"Open src\\/main.ts and look\",\"messageId\":\"sched-2\",\"files\":[]}",
			"decoded": { "text": "Open src/main.ts and look", "messageId": "sched-2", "files": [] },
			"wire": []
		},
		{
